Z||000000||maninblack||11-09-2000||09:36 AM||||have any one purchased Mr. Mike's seatcover<BR>before?.How's the quality and is it easy<BR>to install as a weekend project?.<BR>thx||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||11-09-2000||10:28 AM||||I have Mr.Mikes seats. They are EXCELLENT!<BR>Very high quality. I did my seats in one evening. Depending on the style it takes 2-4 hours to do both seats. The kit comes with EVERYTHING you need. He supplies all items including tools to install the hogrings. The video on how to do it is very well done. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||maninblack||11-09-2000||10:44 AM||||thanks for your info,I will order a set now.<BR>oh, buy the way , any suggestion for the paddings?,or just make some out from an fome<BR>shop?.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Oreif||11-09-2000||10:53 AM||||Like I said above Mr. Mikes seat comes with everything. He even supplies extra padding for the bottom and seat back plus he supplies cotton wadding to fill the bolsters.<BR>In the kit is:<BR>Leather seat skins<BR>hogrings (more than enough to do the job)<BR>hogring tools (yes 2 of them)<BR>extra foam (4 pieces)<BR>cotton wadding (for the bolsters)<BR>razor blades<BR>spray glue<BR>detailed sheet on how to repair a damaged seat.<BR>Instruction video.<P>You can't go wrong with Mr. Mikes seats.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSC00011.jpg"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-09-2000).]||||reg||1
